/*
A branding component can ship a stylesheet (like this one)
which is applied to parts of the Calamares user-interface.
In principle, all parts can be styled through CSS.
Missing parts should be filed as issues.

The IDs are based on the object names in the C++ code.
You can use the Debug Dialog to find out object names:
  - Open the debug dialog
  - Choose tab *Tools*
  - Click *Widget Tree* button
The list of object names is printed in the log.

Documentation for styling Qt Widgets through a stylesheet
can be found at
    https://doc.qt.io/qt-5/stylesheet-examples.html
    https://doc.qt.io/qt-5/stylesheet-reference.html
In Calamares, styling widget classes is supported (e.g.
using `QComboBox` as a selector).

This example stylesheet has all the actual styling commented out.
The examples are not exhaustive.

*/

/*** Generic Widgets.
 *
 * You can style **all** widgets of a given class by selecting
 * the class name. Some widgets have specialized sub-selectors.
 */

/*
QPushButton { background-color: green; }
*/

/*** Main application window.
 *
 * The main application window has the sidebar, which in turn
 * contains a logo and a list of items -- note that the list
 * can **not** be styled, since it has its own custom C++
 * delegate code.
 */

#mainApp {
    background-color: #15110E;
}

/*
#sidebarApp { }
#logoApp { }
*/

QWidget {
    font: 13px;
    color: #FFF3E6;
    background-color: #15110E;
}

/* Popups (the "Continue with Installation?" confirmation, the error
 * dialog, etc.) are separate top-level QDialog/QMessageBox windows --
 * the blanket QWidget rule above covers their child labels/buttons but
 * not reliably the dialog's own root background in every Qt version, so
 * these are named explicitly too. */
QDialog, QMessageBox {
    background-color: #15110E;
}

QLineEdit, QComboBox, QSpinBox, QPlainTextEdit, QTextEdit, QListView, QTreeView {
    background-color: #241A13;
    color: #FFF3E6;
    border: 1px solid #C97932;
}

QPushButton {
    background-color: #302217;
    color: #FFF3E6;
    border: 1px solid #C97932;
    padding: 4px 10px;
}

QPushButton:hover {
    background-color: #C97932;
}

QPushButton:disabled {
    background-color: #241A13;
    color: #D7C1AA;
    border: 1px solid #5A4230;
}

QDialogButtonBox {
    dialogbuttonbox-buttons-have-icons: 0;
}

#debugButton {
    background-color: none;
    font: bold 8px;
    color: #ffffff;
    height: 32px;
    padding: 0px;
    border: none;
}

/*** Welcome module.
 *
 * There are plenty of parts, but the buttons are the most interesting
 * ones (donate, release notes, ...). The little icon image can be
 * styled through *qproperty-icon*, which is a little obscure.
 * URLs can reference the QRC paths of the Calamares application
 * or loaded via plugins or within the filesystem. There is no
 * comprehensive list of available icons, though.
 */

#aboutButton {
    background-color: none;
    font: 14px;
    border: none;
}

/*
QPushButton#aboutButton { qproperty-icon: url(:/data/images/release.svg); }
#donateButton,
#supportButton,
#releaseNotesButton,
#knownIssuesButton { qproperty-icon: url(:/data/images/help.svg); }
*/

/*** Partitioning module.
 *
 * Many moving parts, which you will need to experiment with.
 */

#scrollAreaWidgetContents {
    background-color: #15110E;
}

QProgressBar {
    background-color: #241A13;
    border: 1px solid #5A4230;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #FFF3E6;
    text-align: center;
}

QProgressBar::chunk {
    background-color: #C97932;
    border-radius: 3px;
}

QCheckBox::indicator:checked, QRadioButton::indicator:checked {
    background-color: #C97932;
    border: 1px solid #F0B46A;
}

QWidget:focus {
    border-color: #F0B46A;
}

QLabel#statusLabel[severity="warning"] {
    color: #D6A25F;
}

/*** Licensing module.
 *
 * The licensing module paints individual widgets for each of
 * the licenses. The item can be collapsed or expanded.
 */

/*
#licenseItem {  }
#licenseItemFullText {  }
*/
